  "verbalization": "Avicin G appears to have a shared target of Fibrinogen beta chain across multiple paths, with each of these targets ultimately linking to GR-ST. This suggests a potential mechanism where Avicin G influences the Fibrinogen beta chain, which in turn interacts with GR-ST. The evidence indicates that Avicin G may act through a common intermediary pathway, where the Fibrinogen beta chain serves as a bridge to GR-ST. The varying targets—such as 2-Prop-1-en-2-yl-2,3-dihydro-1-benzofuran-5-carbaldehyde, Phenylethyl resorcinol, and 5-Hydroxy-2-Nonylchromen-4-One—highlight the possibility of multiple molecular interactions, but all converge on GR-ST. The integration of these pathways suggests that Avicin G may exert its effects through a complex network of molecular interactions, with Fibrinogen beta chain playing a central role in mediating its relationship with GR-ST. The evidence supports a mechanism where Avicin G influences the Fibrinogen beta chain, which then interacts with GR-ST, potentially through a series of biochemical steps that are not fully elucidated.",
